'' T61, RUN: '#if typeof( name )' of a variable, a pointer, a typedef, an enum and a UDT
'' -- POINT is a keyword -- answers as fbc-modern does: the parser tells the preprocessor
'' each declaration's type as it finishes it. It was TKO0308. The two WRONG lines must
'' not print: 'long ptr' is not 'long', nor 'long' 'integer'.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/pp-typeof-var.bas -o tests/codegen/pptypeof.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/pptypeof.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: n long
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pn long ptr
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pt Point
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: pt Alias_
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ml long
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: sh Shade
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: s string
